title: Remembering and working things out
card: Chapter 2 | Remembering things | Names, numbers, text, and working things out
say:
  Programs need to remember things. In Stellanova, you give a value a name with the word set.
uncard

new: shop.stella
type:
  genesis:
    set price to 4.5
    set count to 3
    set total to price times count
    scrawl "Three cakes cost ", total
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 1-5
spot: lines 2-3
say:
  Set price to four point five. Set count to three.
  A name is made the first time it's set, and it can be several words long, like best score or cake price.
spot: line 4
say:
  Total is price times count. Numbers can be added with plus, taken away with minus, multiplied with times, and divided with divided by.
  The symbols plus, minus, star and slash work too, if you like them better.
spot: line 5
say: And scrawl can show several things one after another, with commas between them.
spot: off
run
zoom: output
say: Three cakes cost thirteen and a half.
wait
zoom: out

say: There are many ways to work numbers out. Let's try a few.
line: 5
type:

    scrawl "With a tip: ", (total times 1.15) rounded to 2 decimal places
    scrawl "The larger is ", larger of 7 and 12
    scrawl "Kept in range: ", clamp 150 between 0 and 100
    scrawl "A dice roll: ", random number from 1 to 6
zoom: lines 6-9
spot: line 6
say:
  Rounded to two decimal places rounds a number. The brackets say exactly what belongs together: the total times one point one five, and then that is rounded.
spot: line 7
say: Larger of, and smaller of, pick one of two numbers.
spot: line 8
say: Clamp keeps a number inside a range. A hundred and fifty, kept between zero and a hundred, is a hundred.
spot: line 9
say: And random number from one to six rolls a dice. Both ends can come up.
spot: off
run
zoom: output
say: Here they all are. The dice roll will be different every time.
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 2 | Text | Words between quote marks
say: Text has its own words too.
uncard
clear
type:
  genesis:
    set name to "Ada Lovelace"
    scrawl upper case of name
    scrawl "Her name has ", the size of name, " letters."
    scrawl name begins with "Ada"
    scrawl replace "Lovelace" with "L." in name
    scrawl "Next year she turns " plus (36 plus 1)
    scrawl "42" as a number plus 8
    scrawl 1234567 with commas
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 2-9
spot: line 3
say: Upper case of name gives it in capitals. Lower case of gives small letters.
spot: line 4
say: The size of text is how many letters it has.
spot: line 5
say: Begins with, and ends with, answer yes or no. That's a third kind of value: yes or no.
spot: line 6
say: Replace changes every copy of one piece of text into another.
spot: line 7
say: Plus joins text together, and a number joined to text is written out.
spot: line 8
say: As a number turns text like forty two into a number you can add to. As text goes the other way.
spot: line 9
say: And with commas writes big numbers the way people read them.
spot: off
run
zoom: output
wait
say: Each line did what it said.
zoom: out

card: Chapter 2 | Kinds of values | Numbers, text, and yes or no
say:
  So a name can hold a number, text, or yes or no. Once a name holds one kind, it keeps that kind.
  Let's see what happens if we break that rule.
uncard
clear
type:
  genesis:
    set count to 3
    set count to "three"
  and the universe said i love you
run: expect a mistake
zoom: output
say:
  Stellanova finds the mistake before the program even starts, and says it plainly:
  count holds a number, not text. It even says which line.
wait
zoom: out
say: Mistakes in spelling are found the same way.
clear
type:
  genesis:
    set score to 3
    scrawl scroe
  and the universe said i love you
run: expect a mistake
zoom: output
say: I don't know scroe. Did you mean score? Every mistake is written in plain words like this.
wait
zoom: out
